1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,961
Every week, someone opens a Jira work item

2
00:00:04,001 --> 00:00:07,637
that quietly changes how a company handles
personal data.

3
00:00:07,677 --> 00:00:11,314
A session replay tool here. A new
messaging vendor there.

4
00:00:11,354 --> 00:00:16,157
Nobody meant to skip the privacy review.
It just wasn't part of the workflow.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,282
And when a review does happen, it is an
email thread and a thumbs-up.

6
00:00:22,322 --> 00:00:25,580
Weeks later, the work changes. New data, a
new vendor.

7
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,888
And the old approval still says yes.

8
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:33,984
Article25 is privacy review that lives
inside Jira,

9
00:00:34,024 --> 00:00:36,857
and actually enforces the decision.

10
00:00:36,897 --> 00:00:40,081
Detect. Review. Decide. Enforce. Record.

11
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:45,117
An administrator installs it,

12
00:00:45,157 --> 00:00:49,526
and Get started shows exactly what is left
to do, checked live.

13
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:53,744
Installing protects nothing by itself, so
Article25 says so,

14
00:00:53,784 --> 00:00:57,643
until a workflow transition carries the
Article25 gate.

15
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:02,227
A developer files a work item:

16
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:06,358
add session replay to checkout, with a
vendor called Fernwick.

17
00:01:06,398 --> 00:01:11,217
Article25 reads the text and flags it.
Health data. Systematic monitoring.

18
00:01:11,257 --> 00:01:14,376
A data protection impact assessment is
likely.

19
00:01:14,416 --> 00:01:17,900
Every finding quotes the exact words it is
based on.

20
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:22,577
Each result says whether it came from
AI-assisted or rule-based checks.

21
00:01:22,617 --> 00:01:24,339
This one is rule-based.

22
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:29,865
The privacy reviewer opens it in the
review desk.

23
00:01:29,905 --> 00:01:33,161
The text is on the left, the evidence in
the margin.

24
00:01:33,201 --> 00:01:35,831
Select a finding, and its words light up.

25
00:01:35,871 --> 00:01:39,127
She approves with conditions: mask every
form input,

26
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:41,286
and keep prescription pages out.

27
00:01:41,326 --> 00:01:44,639
The decision is bound to this exact text,
and signed.

28
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:51,027
The developer who reported it cannot
approve their own work.

29
00:01:51,067 --> 00:01:54,229
Article25 explains why, and what to do
instead.

30
00:01:56,270 --> 00:02:00,057
Jira's workflow now asks Article25 before
work can start.

31
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:03,277
Without an approval, the transition is
refused,

32
00:02:03,317 --> 00:02:06,193
and the developer is told what to do next.

33
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:13,830
Teams can start in Monitoring, where
nothing is blocked and Article25 records

34
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:18,247
what it would have stopped, then switch to
Enforcing when they are ready.

35
00:02:18,287 --> 00:02:21,713
Settings shows exactly which transitions
carry the gate.

36
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:25,855
Then the work changes.

37
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:30,901
Someone adds one sentence: send shopper
email addresses to an SMS provider.

38
00:02:30,941 --> 00:02:35,886
Article25 checks the new text, finds
contact data that was never reviewed,

39
00:02:35,926 --> 00:02:38,752
and invalidates the approval on its own.

40
00:02:38,792 --> 00:02:42,926
The gate closes again, until a reviewer
looks at what is new.

41
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:49,482
Every decision becomes a signed record in
a hash chain.

42
00:02:49,522 --> 00:02:54,199
An administrator can verify the whole
history, and export a signed archive.

43
00:02:54,239 --> 00:02:58,566
Anyone can check that archive offline,
with nothing but a public key.

44
00:02:58,606 --> 00:03:01,653
Change a single word, and the verifier
says so.

45
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:07,954
Uninstalling a Forge app deletes its data.

46
00:03:07,994 --> 00:03:12,157
Article25 restores the signed archive into
a fresh install,

47
00:03:12,197 --> 00:03:16,425
verifies the entire chain, and checks
every work item again.

48
00:03:16,465 --> 00:03:19,335
Only approvals of unchanged text count.

49
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:26,552
Under the hood, Forge triggers and queues
check every change.

50
00:03:26,592 --> 00:03:29,925
A versioned rules engine sets each
outcome,

51
00:03:29,965 --> 00:03:34,262
and an optional AI step must quote the
text it relies on.

52
00:03:34,302 --> 00:03:38,668
The workflow validator reads only
Article25's own records,

53
00:03:38,708 --> 00:03:41,972
and every decision is signed with Ed25519.

54
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:46,823
Article25.

55
00:03:46,863 --> 00:03:50,575
Privacy review that actually enforces the
decision.

56
00:03:50,615 --> 00:03:54,986
Built entirely on Atlassian Forge, with no
external services.
